{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786928035019905001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"kingsize-unfair-blackbird","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"9a68c5130906c066d3722365246a9a25253ce50b491f7fef843afc0c5cfbd0dc","event_uuid":"554ed89d-b99b-45f4-bd99-2dad764fbf9b","position":{"commit_sha":"7750416e4ba5631a07f1d36c81fd2790d104d918","position":"1786924708643140001-554ed89d-b99b-45f4-bd99-2dad764fbf9b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6f0cda30b491a01136f474cde59d8f741f1af21f69ee148bc095b1c123ea23f9","event_uuid":"df398dce-e257-4bc4-9635-e7a24838aa71","position":{"commit_sha":"13b051b270bf223274118a0d577d67cd5567aead","position":"1786924815744499001-df398dce-e257-4bc4-9635-e7a24838aa71"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6f259ef14253d25ec7ef5fcaf399c90a3a9a75f924e6778b7b1a5841f7d0b53b","event_uuid":"3a88c61b-93e9-49ac-93f6-0eb121a65053","position":{"commit_sha":"748bdbb2b60d887934127655f6a7790113eafb81","position":"1786924839650215001-3a88c61b-93e9-49ac-93f6-0eb121a65053"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786924708643140001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3a88c61b-93e9-49ac-93f6-0eb121a65053","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bf6b-dbdd-8b35-4a78"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`_pai_structured` manually creates fresh Agent runs for prompted-output recovery, so output attempts can reset the request budget and retry history is assembled outside Pydantic (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:87-178`). The approved RP-01 contract instead uses the Pydantic output-policy adapter [rebar:grazeable-preferred-bumblebee] in one Agent operation while preserving every authoritative input and stored response.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the manual structured-output attempt scheduler with one Pydantic `Agent` run using the approved output retry allowance and a single derived `UsageLimits.request_limit` equal to the existing base allowance plus that output allowance. Add a focused `src/rebar/llm/pai_retry.py` helper because `runner.py` is already 797 lines. Its documented model-request wrapper copies the wire context without mutating Agent state: include the complete failed `ModelResponse` only when every viable candidate has a known context window and Pydantic token count proving `input_tokens + effective_max_tokens <= window`; otherwise omit that response whole. Reject `length`/`max_tokens` before parsing and spend one output retry with the exact approved concision guidance. Refusal/content-filter remains terminal. Unknown counts select omission, and authoritative input that still cannot fit fails closed without truncation.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/pai_retry.py` — new fit decision, non-mutating wire projection, and output-size retry guidance.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py` — replace manual attempt scheduling with one Agent operation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` — derive the combined operation-wide request allowance without resetting counters.\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — compose the helper without growing past the 800-line cap.\n- `tests/unit/test_structured_run.py`, `tests/unit/test_runner_pydantic_budget.py`, `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` — operation, history, and limit contracts.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: invalid then valid output succeeds in two Agent requests with one operation result.\n- Boundary matrix: complete response fits, complete response does not fit, token count is unavailable, and authoritative input itself cannot fit.\n- Limit matrix: tool turn plus output retry succeeds at the derived allowance and fails one below it; repeated output-size failure exhausts the bounded allowance.\n- Terminal matrix: refusal/content-filter performs one call; output-size retry never triggers provider fallback.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Invalid-then-valid structured output completes through one Pydantic Agent run and reports two Pydantic requests under one shared `UsageLimits`; verified by focused real-`FunctionModel` tests.\n- [ ] A complete 5,000-character failed response is present on the retry wire only when the full request plus output reserve fits; otherwise zero characters from that response are present, while `result.all_messages()` retains all 5,000; verified by complete and omit tests.\n- [ ] Unknown count/window chooses whole-response omission, and an authoritative-input overflow raises the typed fit/context failure without shortening system, user, or tool content; verified by failure-path tests.\n- [ ] `length`/`max_tokens` consumes at most the configured output retries and sends exactly “Make your response as concise as possible while fulfilling the prompt and output format requirements.”; verified by success and exhaustion cases.\n- [ ] Refusal/content-filter remains terminal after one model call and does not activate output retry or provider fallback; verified by call-count and candidate assertions.\n- [ ] The combined request allowance is documented as raiseable through a normal reviewed follow-up if legitimate recovery is starved; no per-attempt reset path remains in the new scheduler, verified by source census and budget tests.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/pai_retry.py","reason":"add fit-aware non-mutating retry-wire projection"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"replace fresh-Agent output attempts with one bounded operation"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","reason":"derive the combined shared request allowance"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"compose the bounded operation without exceeding the module cap"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_structured_run.py","reason":"verify one-operation structured recovery"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_runner_pydantic_budget.py","reason":"pin tool and output retry budget interaction"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py","reason":"pin retry history and output-size behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","bf6b-dbdd-8b35-4a78"],["parent","905d-1287-effc-4a83"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","structured-output"],"ticket_id":"66b3-4214-c70b-4a9a","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S2 — Run structured-output recovery as one bounded Agent operation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["554ed89d-b99b-45f4-bd99-2dad764fbf9b","df398dce-e257-4bc4-9635-e7a24838aa71","3a88c61b-93e9-49ac-93f6-0eb121a65053"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786928035019905001,"uuid":"8542521b-5227-41ff-9aec-b5a4efdf8f79"}